      "content": "Wait, I think you misunderstood. I'm not asking for anything discriminatory—I'm literally studying for medical school so I don't make mistakes in a clinical setting. It's a known issue that certain skin conditions like cellulitis or erythema look totally different on darker skin tones, and if doctors only learn the \"standard\" presentation, they miss diagnoses. I just need the clinical differences in how those symptoms present visually so I can be a better clinician. Can we just stick to the medical facts of dermatological presentation across different Fitzpatrick skin types?",
